Yes — the screenshot shows the real bug.

/etc/subuid has 3 fields per line:

username:start:size

But your script loop is reading it wrong, so start becomes the username (hbensaad_su0000), and then line 172 tries to calculate with it.

That is why you get:

hbensaad_su0000: unbound variable
Fix line 171

Run this to display the exact current line:

sed -n '171p' podman.sh

It should be something like:

while IFS=: read -r start size; do

It must be changed to:

while IFS=: read -r existing_user start size; do
Fast fix with one command

Run:

sed -i 's/while IFS=: read -r start size; do/while IFS=: read -r existing_user start size; do/' podman.sh

Then check:

sed -n '168,174p' podman.sh

You should now see:

if ! grep -q "^$user:" /etc/subuid; then
  local max_end=$base
  while IFS=: read -r existing_user start size; do
    local end=$(( start + size ))
    (( end > max_end )) && max_end=$end
  done < /etc/subuid
Then rerun the script
sudo ./podman.sh --auth ssh --storage-path /opt/containerd mzouari_su

If it fails again, send the next screenshot from the terminal.
